{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And they shall abandon.</b> The alef is superfluous, and the meaning is יזנחום, men shall abandon them." "<b>They shall dry up.</b> From the root דל (Leviticus 34:21)." "<b>The rivers of Matsor.</b> The rivers, [called by this name] because the enemy will not be able to cut them off when he comes into the land in a siege." "<b>Reed and rush.</b> Plants on the bank of the river." "<b>They have withered.</b> They are cut down, and [this word] is joined with סוף in the verse itself (Isaiah 33:9)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {1 "The citation ל\"ד is likely a misprint or error for the standard chapter numbering; Leviticus 21 has no verse matching this root."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:19.088110939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}